.TH smi-jenkins-node "1" "August 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Server Command"
.SH NAME
smi-jenkins-node \- Connect this machine to a Jenkins controller as an agent node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-jenkins-node
.br
.B smi-jenkins-node
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-workdir
.IR DIR ]
.RI [ AGENT_ARGS\| .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-jenkins-node
connects this machine to a Jenkins controller by running
.BR jenkins-agent.jar .
No options are required for normal use beyond supplying the agent secret
via the
.SM SMI_JENKINS_SECRET
environment variable.
.PP
The wrapper constructs the controller URL and native agent options
.RB ( \-url ,
.BR \-secret ,
.BR \-name ,
.BR \-webSocket )
automatically from environment variables and defaults.
The user does not need to know or supply those options.
.PP
The agent secret must be provided via the
.SM SMI_JENKINS_SECRET
environment variable only.
There is no
.B \-\-secret
option; secrets must not appear in shell history or process argument lists.
.PP
Any Jenkins agent arguments supplied after the wrapper options are passed
through unchanged.
.PP
JVM options may be supplied via the
.SM JAVA_OPTS
environment variable.
.SH MODES
.PP
The script selects its JAR and nodes root automatically from the effective
user name, so the same command works on a developer workstation and on a
live installation.
.TP
.B jenkins
Live installation (rpm package, container image).
The agent JAR is
.BR /usr/share/java/jenkins-agent.jar
when that file exists, otherwise the one reported by
.BR smi-lib-location (1),
and the nodes root is
.BI $JENKINS_HOME /nodes\fR,
falling back to the jenkins user home directory when
.SM JENKINS_HOME
is not set.
.TP
.B any other user
Development.
The agent JAR is located via
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
and the nodes root is
.BR ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins/nodes .
.PP
The working directory of a node is the
.I NAME
subdirectory of the nodes root, so several nodes may run side by side
without further configuration.
It is created when it does not exist.
.SH INSTALLATION
.PP
In development mode the agent JAR is the one installed by the
.B jenkins
package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
smi-download-package jenkins
smi-install-package jenkins
.fi
.RE
.PP
.BR smi-install-package (1)
places
.BR jenkins.war ,
.B jenkins-cli.jar
and
.B jenkins-agent.jar
as root into the directory reported by
.BR smi-lib-location (1),
which is
.B /opt/setmy.info/lib
in a normal installation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Controller host.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_HOST
and the built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Controller port.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_PORT
and the built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Node name registered in Jenkins.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_NODE_NAME
and the hostname default.
.TP
.BI \-\-workdir " DIR"
Agent working directory.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_WORKDIR
and the built-in default.
Passed as
.B \-workDir
to the agent JAR.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.PP
All other arguments are passed directly to
.BR jenkins-agent.jar .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_SECRET
Agent secret token.
.B Required.
No default.
Never supply this via command-line options.
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_HOST
Controller host.
Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_PORT
Controller port.
Default:
.BR 7070 .
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_NODE_NAME
Node name.
Default: output of
.BR hostname (1).
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_WORKDIR
Agent working directory.
Default: the node directory
.IR NAME
under the nodes root of the active mode.
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_AGENT
Agent JAR file.
Default: mode dependent, see
.BR MODES .
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_HOME
Jenkins home directory, development mode only.
The nodes root is the
.B nodes
directory below it, so a controller started with a non-default home keeps
its nodes together with its own data.
Default:
.BR ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins .
.TP
.B JAVA_OPTS
Additional JVM options.
.SH PRECEDENCE
.PP
.B --host
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_HOST
> 127.0.0.1
.PP
.B --port
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_PORT
> 7070
.PP
.B --name
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_NODE_NAME
> hostname
.PP
.B --workdir
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_WORKDIR
> NODES_DIR/NAME
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Connect with all defaults (secret from environment):
.RS
.B SMI_JENKINS_SECRET=abc123 smi-jenkins-node
.RE
.PP
Connect with environment configuration (suitable for systemd):
.RS
.nf
SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_HOST=192.168.1.10
SMI_JENKINS_CONTROLLER_PORT=8080
SMI_JENKINS_NODE_NAME=linux-build-01
SMI_JENKINS_SECRET=abc123
.fi
.RS
.B smi-jenkins-node
.RE
.RE
.PP
Override node name on the command line:
.RS
.B SMI_JENKINS_SECRET=abc123 smi-jenkins-node --name build-01
.RE
.PP
Run two nodes on one developer workstation:
.RS
.nf
SMI_JENKINS_SECRET=abc123 smi-jenkins-node --name build-01
SMI_JENKINS_SECRET=def456 smi-jenkins-node --name build-02
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins/nodes
Nodes root in development mode.
.TP
.BI ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins/nodes/ NAME
Work directory of a single node.
Created when it does not exist.
.TP
.B /opt/setmy.info/lib/jenkins-agent.jar
Agent JAR used in development mode, installed by
.BR smi-install-package (1).
.TP
.B /usr/share/java/jenkins-agent.jar
Agent JAR used in live mode when present.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-jenkins-controller (1),
.BR jenkins-cli (1),
.BR smi-download-package (1),
.BR smi-install-package (1),
.BR smi-home-location (1),
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
